{"metadata":{"description":"Read-only recovery drill evidence for DeepSeek Harness","id":"gh:1333626396","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-recovery-proof","slug":"dongsheng123132/dsh-recovery-proof","topics":["ai-agent","deepseek-harness","disaster-recovery","dsh","dsh-plugin","evidence","recovery-testing"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Read-only recovery drill evidence for DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# DSH Recovery Proof"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Maintainer / Author：He Fangsheng (贺方升 / 贺去病; also known as Dosen) · hequbing.com**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A read-only recovery-drill evidence verifier for DeepSeek Harness. It does **not** restore files, cr"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"eate checkpoints, or replace recovery executors such as Turn Rewind or Checkpoint Rewind. It verifie"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"s that an external drill left reproducible evidence. Version 0.2.0 is also a formal Codex plugin wit"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"h a proof-only MCP server, and its namespace export is regression-tested against the stock DSH Web L"},{"id":"p4s5","text":"oof-only MCP server, and its namespace export is regression-tested against the stock DSH Web Loader."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## What it proves"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"- every referenced prestate, rescue, restored or rollback object is a regular workspace file with th"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"e declared SHA-256 and revision;
- recovery, failed-apply rollback and stale-plan rejection follow t"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"he manifest's exact phase sequence;
- rescue evidence exists before apply, failed apply is followed "},{"id":"p6s4","text":"by successful rollback, and stale plans are rejected;
- accumulated structural event duration remain"},{"id":"p6s5","text":"s within each scenario's RTO threshold;
- missing/stale evidence and every failed rule are disclosed"},{"id":"p6s6","text":" in a content-addressed JSON report."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Inputs are explicit JSON/JSONL files. Secret-, token-, prompt-, chat- and content-shaped fields are "},{"id":"p7s2","text":"rejected. Object contents are never included in output. The verifier writes only to the explicit wor"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"kspace-relative `artifactDir`, using an atomic write and SHA-256 read-back check."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Install and compose"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"The bundle registers `dsh_recovery_proof_inspect` and `dsh_recovery_proof_verify`. The package inten"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"tionally exports a Cordis namespace (`name`, `inject`, `apply`) rather than a default function so th"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"e stock Loader retains the `tools` injection declaration."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## CLI"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Exit code `0` means the command ran and verification passed, `2` means the evidence was processed bu"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"t failed policy, and `1` means invalid or unsafe input."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Manifest and events"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"See `examples/basic`. A manifest pins `system.revision`, content-addressed objects, and explicit sce"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"narios with `expectedPhases`, `requiredObjectIds`, and `maxRtoMs`. Events contain only structural fa"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"cts: unique idempotency key, scenario, sequence, phase, status, duration and object references."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Codex and proof-only MCP"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The repository retains a validated `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` and declares the stdio server in `.mc"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"p.json`. MCP exposes:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"- `recovery_manifest_inspect` for bounded inline manifest validation;
- `recovery_evidence_verify` f"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"or bounded inline JSONL phase/RTO/rollback/stale-plan checks."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Both MCP tools reuse the same validation core as DSH and CLI, but never access the filesystem, deref"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"erence object paths, write an artifact or execute a recovery action. Their result explicitly states "},{"id":"p19s3","text":"that object-content verification was not performed. Use the DSH or CLI surface when object hashes an"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"d the content-addressed report must be verified against a workspace."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Security boundary"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"All input paths and the output directory must remain under `workspaceRoot`; symlink inputs and symli"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"nk output directories are rejected. No shell is spawned, no network is used, no recovery action is e"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"xecuted, and there are no install lifecycle scripts."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":false}
